{#
    The bar. One of them, for every kind of page.

    Its parts are configuration — the mark, the version, the search — and the
    site itself is `menu()`: one entry with every section under it, each with
    its pages, and the page the reader is on marked wherever it sits. The bar
    draws as much of that as the width allows: the front doors in the row, the
    pages of one of them in a panel under it, the whole tree in its drawer.

    Handed over as data rather than written between the tags. This renderer has
    resolved its own tree already, and what the element does with it — measure
    what still fits, fold the rest — needs the list rather than the markup of
    one. What a project sets, and where, is
    `docs/guides-theme/configuration.rst`.
#}
<sds-nav-main
    home="{{ soul.home ? asset(soul.home) : renderLink('/index') }}"
    {%- if soul.signet %} signet="{{ asset('/' ~ soul.signet) }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if soul.brand %} brand="{{ soul.brand }}"{% endif %}
    product="{{ soul.product|default(env.projectNode.title)|default('Documentation') }}"
    {#- No version here. It is a fact about the documentation rather than a
        control, and at this end of the row it takes the room the controls
        need: the footer carries it, on every page alike. -#}
    index="{{ root }}_search.json"
    menu="{{ menu()|json_encode }}"
></sds-nav-main>
